        ":question/problem": "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=4t,\\,\\,\\,y=-{t}^{3},\\,-3\\le t\\le 1,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values:\n\n| **$t$** | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-12$ | $-8$ | $a$ | $b$ | $4$ |\n| $y$ | $27$ | $8$ | $1$ | $0$ | $c$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "- To find the value of $a,$ we substitute $t=-1$ into $x=4t.$ This gives\n\n$$\na=4(-1)=-4.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $b,$ we substitute $t=0$ into $x=4t.$ This gives\n\n$$\nb=4(0)=0.\n$$\n\n- To find the value of $c,$ we substitute $t=1$ into $y=-{t}^{3}.$ This gives\n\n$$\nc=-(1)^{3}=-1.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-4+0+(-1)=-5.\n$$",
